<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Polish–Ottoman War (1620–1621)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1620">1620</a>–<a href="/years/1621">1621</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Polish–Ottoman War of 1620–1621 was fought between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish–Lithuanian Commonwealth</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> over Moldavia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> raids on Ottoman lands. A Polish army was destroyed at Cecora in 1620, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hetman">Hetman</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stanis-aw-zo-kiewski">Stanisław Żółkiewski</a> was killed, but in 1621 Polish and Cossack forces held off Osman II at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khotyn">Khotyn</a>, and the Treaty of Khotyn restored the earlier frontier.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/polish-ottoman-war-1620-1621.jpg" alt="Polish–Ottoman War (1620–1621)" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SebbeKg · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Polish-Ottoman_War_(1620-1621).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
